          "metadata": {
            "stream_source": "live"
          },
          "text": "# Streaming Probe\n\n1. Always record the date and time of each observation immediately.\n2. Use descriptive adjectives to capture the sensory details of the environment.\n3. Avoid interpreting data in the moment to prevent observer bias.\n4. Write in complete sentences to ensure clarity for future analysis.\n5. Note the exact location of the subject relative to fixed landmarks.\n6. Document the weather conditions as they may influence behavior.\n7. Use a consistent shorthand that is defined in a separate key.\n8. Record verbatim quotes whenever a subject speaks.\n9. Describe the physical layout of the space before detailing specific actions.\n10. Maintain a neutral tone throughout the descriptive process.\n11. Distinguish clearly between observed facts and personal reflections.\n12. Note any interruptions or anomalies that occur during the session.\n13. Use a durable notebook or a reliable digital device for data entry.\n14. Review and expand upon shorthand notes as soon as possible after the event.\n15. Document the presence and roles of other people in the vicinity.\n16. Ensure that all handwriting is legible to avoid transcription errors.",
